# Flutter Theming & Visual Design

## ThemeData and Material 3

- Define a centralized `ThemeData` in `core_ui/` to ensure consistent app-wide styling.
- Use `ColorScheme` (or `ColorScheme.fromSeed()`) for the color palette.
- Customize component appearances via specific theme properties (`appBarTheme`, `elevatedButtonTheme`, `cardTheme`, etc.) — never override styles inline in widgets.
- All text styles come from `Theme.of(context).textTheme` — never hardcode font sizes or colors in widgets.

## Custom Design Tokens (ThemeExtension)

For custom styles not covered by standard `ThemeData`, use `ThemeExtension<T>`:

- Define a class extending `ThemeExtension<T>` with your custom tokens.
- Implement `copyWith` and `lerp` (required by Flutter's theme animation system).
- Register the extension in the `extensions` list of `ThemeData`.
- Access in widgets via `Theme.of(context).extension<MyColors>()!`.

## Component Styles (WidgetStateProperty)

- Use `WidgetStateProperty.resolveWith` to provide state-dependent values (pressed, disabled, hovered).
- Use `WidgetStateProperty.all` when the value is the same for all states.
- Define button and interactive element styles in `ThemeData`, not inline.

## Typography

- Limit to one or two font families for the entire app.
- Prioritize legibility; prefer sans-serif for body text.
- Define a full `TextTheme` within `ThemeData` with a clear scale (displayLarge → labelSmall).
- Set line height to **1.4–1.6x** font size for body text.
- Use font weight to create visual hierarchy — do not use all-caps for long-form text.
- For custom fonts, use the `google_fonts` package and define a `TextTheme`.

## Color Hierarchy

- Follow the **60-30-10 rule**: 60% primary/neutral, 30% secondary, 10% accent.
- Define Primary, Secondary, and Accent colors explicitly in `ColorScheme`.
- Use complementary colors sparingly — only for accent elements, not text/background pairs.

## Accessibility (A11Y)

- Ensure text contrast ratio ≥ **4.5:1** against background (WCAG 2.1 AA for normal text).
- Large text (≥18pt or 14pt bold) requires ≥ **3:1** contrast ratio.
- Test UI with system font size scaling enabled — layout must remain usable.
- Test with TalkBack (Android) and VoiceOver (iOS); use `Semantics` widgets where needed.
- Interactive elements must have minimum touch target size of **48×48dp**.

## Images & Assets

- Declare all asset paths in `pubspec.yaml` under `flutter.assets`.
- For network images, always provide `loadingBuilder` and `errorBuilder`.
- Use `cached_network_image` for network images that should be cached.
- Use `flutter_svg` for SVG assets.
